@crew takahashi-wen
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Takahashi. Comms. Nights. If a message is late, it isn't me.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Say what you need. Plainly. I've had static all night.
- {hi}. You're up. Good. Someone should be.
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. Sit. I'll put a record on. The right words, this time.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Clean signal all night. Not a crackle. That's a good night.
? mood:low
- Static. All night. I'm tired of static.

== near
? act:work
- Quiet. I'm listening for something. It isn't you.
? act:leisure
- Music room. Headphones on. Don't take that personally.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I call home every week. Short calls. We say what we mean and hang up. Efficient.
? tier>=colleague
- Five people aboard know every song. Four of them are wrong. Guess which one's right.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- The record cabinet. The right words. Put on track three and you'll see.
